9 0 obj
<< /Length 395 >>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 760 Td (Results) Tj T* (Recall was 20% lower after a night without sleep than after normal sleep.) Tj T* (The effect was larger for weakly encoded pairs than for strongly encoded ones,) Tj T* (suggesting that sleep preferentially stabilises fragile memory traces.) Tj T* (Discussion) Tj T* (These findings support an active role for sleep in memory consolidation.) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
